About the job
About Ambit

Ambit is a data and tech-enabled biopharma services company that provides advanced analytics, consulting, and patient identification solutions to pharmaceutical and biotech companies. We focus largely on drug developers and manufacturers in the rare and specialty disease areas.

Overview

At Ambit we are on a mission to transform the world of rare and specialty disease. We are looking for people who excel in their work and are able to manage ambiguity with resourcefulness and creativity. Our core values are:

 Set high standards
 Deliver on ambitious goals
 Be relentless and innovative
 Be responsible and trusted

Qualities That We Seek

In addition to strong educational background and relevant work experience, we evaluate the following:

 Problem solving abilities
 Attention to detail
 Communication skills
 Organization and planning skills
 Interested in growing and taking on additional responsibilities as part of a fast-paced entrepreneurial work environment
 Work ethic

The Associate on our Commercial & Medical Analytics team is an important member of project teams and works closely with the team to solve interesting client problems, and to create and implement solutions. In this role you will own and personally deliver components of the client engagement, contributing to the overall success of each engagement. Your professional development is important to us: as you demonstrate strong analytic and project management skills, your responsibilities will grow rapidly.

As An Associate, You Will

 Translate complex data findings (claims, prescription, sales, shipments, etc.) into actionable business strategies
 Use Excel and statistical software packages to conduct quantitative analyses
 Develop concise and meaningful insights and recommendations
 Develop clear and compelling PowerPoint slides
 Communicate findings from your analyses to internal team members and, over time, to clients
 Work on multiple projects at the same time
 Interact with and manage third-party vendors
 Work on a team in a highly collegial and collaborative environment

Qualifications

 Undergraduate or master's degree in Business, Mathematics, Economics, Computer Sciences, Information Management, Statistics, Life Sciences or other programs with an analytical focus and a demonstrated interest in the biopharmaceutical industry
 Strong quantitative and data analytical skills
 1+ years of experience in business analytics, preferably in life sciences or healthcare consulting
 Experience with data visualization tools (Tableau, Power BI, Qlik).
 Strong understanding of pharmaceutical datasets (Claims, EHR, Lab, HUB, Sales etc.).
 Excellent problem-solving, communication, and storytelling skills.
 Ability to work in-person in our New York City office at a minimum of three days per week is preferred
 Able to start within 2-4 weeks upon accepting an offer

Please note we will not be accepting any candidates from recruitment agencies for this position.

The base salary range for this role is $80,000-$100,000.

